Theorem CH-103: rc_counting engine bootstrap (bounded-loop RC balance)

  Preconditions:
    - L is a basic block containing a linear loop body that uses
      v exactly once per iteration per Annex E §AIMS TF-11
      (operand demand)
    - the loop runs N iterations with N a finite non-negative
      integer
    - v has Access = Owned and Consumption = Linear at the entry
      of each iteration per the loop invariant
    - rc_counting engine discharges per-instruction RC-delta
      arithmetic over integers per the foundational-axiom policy
      sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape
    - the goal is to bound the total number of RcInc and RcDec
      operations emitted by the realization phase for v across N
      iterations

  Soundness property:
    Forall N in nat.
      (the linear loop iterates N times) implies
      (the number of RcInc operations on v plus the number of
       RcDec operations on v across the N iterations is at most
       2 * N + 2);
      i.e. each iteration contributes at most one RcInc and one
        RcDec pair; the loop entry and exit contribute at most
        one additional RcInc and RcDec pair; the bound is
        deterministic and finite.

  Proof obligation:
    Structural induction on N with per-iteration RC-delta
    arithmetic per the rc_counting engine.

      Base case (N = 0):
        Loop body executes zero times. RC contribution from the
        body is zero. Loop entry RcInc (if any) and loop exit
        RcDec (if any) bound by 2 (the entry and exit pair).
        Total RC ops at most 2; satisfies 2 * 0 + 2 = 2.

      Inductive step (assume bound holds at N; prove at N + 1):
        Inductive hypothesis: at N iterations the bound is
        2 * N + 2.
        Extending to N + 1 iterations executes the body one more
        time. The body uses v once per the linear-loop invariant;
        per Annex E §AIMS TF-11 standard demand
        (operand, cardinality = Once, consumption = Linear), the
        realization phase emits at most one RcInc and one RcDec
        for the body's use of v per iteration (RL-1 and RL-2).
        Therefore the (N + 1) iteration adds at most 2 RC ops to
        the running total: 2 * N + 2 + 2 = 2 * (N + 1) + 2.

    RC-balance equation witness:
      Define balance(k) = (count of RcInc on v in iterations 0..k)
        minus (count of RcDec on v in iterations 0..k).
      At iteration boundaries (entry of each iteration), balance
        is zero by the loop invariant: every RcInc inserted in the
        body is paired with an RcDec before the next iteration.
      At loop exit, balance is zero plus the optional entry-exit
        adjustment (at most one inc-dec pair).
      Therefore total inc + dec count is bounded by 2 * N + 2;
      no unbalanced sequence escapes.

    Closed-world coverage:
      Every loop iteration is one of N copies of the same body;
      the per-iteration RC contribution is bounded by 2 (RL-1 plus
      RL-2 for a single use). Entry and exit contribute at most 2
      additional ops. No other instruction in the loop body emits
      RC ops on v (TF-2 Let Var transparent alias; TF-4 Project is
      a borrow not a use; TF-N/A RcInc and RcDec themselves do not
      emit recursive RC).

    Lattice validation:
      Consumption = Linear is preserved across loop iterations per
      the loop invariant; Access = Owned is preserved; Cardinality
      accumulates via seq_add (Once + Once = Many) inside the loop
      body when the same value is used multiple times within one
      iteration, but the linear-loop precondition restricts the
      body to exactly one use per iteration. CN-1 (Dead implies
      Absent) does not fire at any iteration entry because
      Consumption = Linear is not equal to Dead.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (per-iteration RC-delta arithmetic; balance
                   equation witness; structural induction on N)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: 01A bootstrap discharged via §01A Implementation Items (engine constructive verification + Lean 4 cross-validation)
